Z||000006||Fformula88||11-28-2001||03:45 PM||||I don't think it should come as any surprise that the MR2 board would be biased and flame Fiero's.  They love their MR2's as much as people here love Fiero's.  It doesn't bother me.  In fact, I also like MR2's.  The MkII's with the turbo are very fast!  The MkII's also look great IMO (MkI=not so hot).<P>I also don't think its very fair to directly compare the MkII with the Fiero since it is a redesign of the original... something the Fiero was not fortunate enough to get.  But to each his own!  <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000007||LoW_KeY||11-28-2001||03:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pyric:<BR><B>I found they stop laughing when they realize they have the gas to the floor and they're STILL looking at MY tail lights.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <P>Heh, heh.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh yeah.. I've had a few encounters guy was laughing and I was like man sorry to be you, then I show'd him the power of the V6  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> but hey there are a lot of nice cars out there.. I know not all people are bad who own them, I run into a lot of mustang guys that like my car.<BR><P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kcbanner.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||AusFiero||11-28-2001||05:20 PM||||Ok I can be unbias here because I own a 86 Fiero GT Fastback and a Series II MR2 GT. Sorry to say guys. The MR2 beats the Fiero in all areas except external looks and the fact it is easier to modify.<BR>I don't know about American version MR2s but the ones released in Australia have more horsepower than the Fiero, non turbo. The turboes just kick our asses. They brake better, handle better and have a nicer interior. <BR>But I still prefer my Fiero because it looks more Ferrarish and is pretty rare over here.<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000009||stimpy||11-28-2001||05:47 PM||||What was so bad about that? I read the thread and did not see one comment that I felt was unjustifiable or un-called for. There are actually several positive comments, such as;<BR>"they (fiero and their owners) are our brothern. We should not bash eachother."<P>"I wouldn't mind owning a Fieros (sic)GT."<P>"I think if you ask members that are old enough to have owned a Fiero back in 84 then you would get a different oppinion. I very much doubt that the MR2 would have been sold here if it weren't for the Pontiac. <BR>I like the old cars.. I really like the GT version... I would love to have one to plop a Caddie v8 into one. That would be fun. <BR>I really think the Fiero community is pretty tight. <BR>The spaceframe design was well ahead of the times also."<P>"I respect the owners and the car enough not to talk badly about them."<P> What's the point of this thread, anyhow? Are you trying to get people riled up to go over and flame the MR2 owners? If so, grow up. This little battle has been done to death before, and I hope it doesn't go there again.<P>||||reg||5
Z||000010||Ryan Wright||11-28-2001||08:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>They brake better, handle better and have a nicer interior. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I owned an '85 MR-2 before I bought my Fiero (at least 7 years ago); the interior wasn't anywhere near as nice as the Fiero, and neither was the exterior.<P>However, your comments about braking and handling are dead on. That car ran circles around my Fiero in that department. Even my new GT with custom suspension & rear sway bar, etc, wouldn't keep up with my '85 MR-2 in that department. Of course, with the 3800SC in the back, my Fiero would stop any MR-2 into the ground in the acceleration department.<P>I enjoyed my MR-2 and while I'd never trade my Fiero for one, I wouldn't mind owning another. It was a fun little car for the ~2 years I had it and was my first sports car.<P>Last but not least, flaming someone over their choice of car is, well, childish and immature. Responding to other's flames is just as bad. Get over it.<P>------------------<BR>-Ryan Wright (http://www.ryanwright.com)||||reg||1
